<Project>

  <!-- ================================================================
       Workaround: disable the broken Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0.x
       XmlComment source-generator.
       ================================================================

       The generator emits literal `mediaType.Example = jsonString.Parse();`
       against `IOpenApiMediaType.Example`, which Microsoft.OpenApi 3.x
       made interface-readonly. Bowire core pulls in Microsoft.OpenApi
       3.5.3 transitively via Kuestenlogik.Bowire.Protocol.Rest, so
       any sample that adds `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` (for
       AddOpenApi / MapOpenApi) gets the broken generated file and
       fails to compile with CS0200.

       Tracking issues (opened Nov 2025, no fix yet as of May 2026):
         - https://github.com/microsoft/OpenAPI.NET/issues/2582
         - https://github.com/microsoft/OpenAPI.NET/issues/2610
         - https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/64317

       Microsoft's own statement: ".NET 10 does not provide full support
       for Microsoft.OpenApi 3.x, broader support is expected in a
       future .NET release."

       What this target does: removes the SourceGenerators DLL from the
       analyzer set before CoreCompile. The runtime types (AddOpenApi,
       MapOpenApi, transformer interfaces) come from a different DLL in
       the same package and stay available — so endpoints still discover,
       schemas still generate, only the auto-XML-doc-comment-harvesting
       step is skipped.

       What we lose: <summary>/<remarks>/<param> XML doc comments on
       controller actions no longer auto-flow into /openapi/v1.json.
       Workaround on the affected endpoints (only a handful in this
       repo): use `MapGet(...).WithSummary("...").WithDescription("...")`
       which goes through a different code path and is unaffected.

       To remove this workaround once Microsoft fixes the source-gen:
       just delete this whole <Target> element. The condition is a
       no-op for projects that don't reference Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi.
       ================================================================ -->
  <Target Name="WorkaroundOpenApiBrokenSourceGenerator" BeforeTargets="CoreCompile">
    <ItemGroup>
      <Analyzer Remove="@(Analyzer)"
                Condition="'%(Filename)%(Extension)' == 'Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi.SourceGenerators.dll'" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
